# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Next reads it at boot, so restart `next dev` after changing.

# Where the backend is. Unset (or the file absent) and the app runs entirely on the in-process
# mock engine: no backend, no network, twelve hand-written venues. That is a supported mode,
# not a broken one — it is what makes the prototype open on a laptop with no connection.
#
#   local     http://localhost:8000
#   deployed  https://haazir-api.fly.dev
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is not a secret prefix. Everything under it is compiled into the browser bundle
# and visible to anyone who opens devtools, so nothing private belongs here — which is why the
# database URL, the JWT secret and the provider keys all live on the API and never in this app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_HAAZIR_API=
